1
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:06,290
After New Year, entrance exams
for private schools will finally begin.

2
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:09,140
Make sure you keep studying until then.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,640
Winter break starts next week.

4
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:15,610
I'm going to graduate soon!

5
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,610
T-there's no time left!

6
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:22,890
So what's this important stuff
you're going to talk about?

7
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:24,400
Listen carefully.

8
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:28,060
Kijibayashi and I will graduate
in three months.

9
00:00:28,190 --> 00:00:30,570
There will only be
Inukawa and Saruta left.

10
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:33,840
That would naturally mean Brainwave Club
is going to be terminated.

11
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:36,640
Isn't that just sad?

12
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:39,510
-What's so sad about it?
-Huh?

13
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:42,550
We're not going to make
any memories at this rate.

14
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:45,120
Think back to everything we did so far!

15
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:49,010
But we have some memories,

16
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:51,320
like eating snacks and chatting
while lazing around.

17
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:53,850
There's also playing cards and games.

18
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:56,360
No, I'm not talking about
that kind of stuff.

19
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:57,224
-Huh?
-Huh?

20
00:00:57,650 --> 00:00:59,250
Huh?

21
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,080
Wait, what?

22
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:11,550
Why are you crying?

23
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:13,310
Is your stomach hurting?

24
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:15,480
Did your exam go that badly?

25
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,140
I mean, I'm no better, but...

26
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:20,510
We didn't make any progress
on our research for telepathy!

27
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:22,290
This is our only chance!

28
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:24,110
Is it something worth crying over?

29
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:26,920
Y-you can try better
at high school, right?

30
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:31,740
So, you were actually serious about
wanting to communicate with aliens?

31
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,070
Of course I am...

32
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:36,790
I'm also going to continue it as a hobby.

33
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:41,330
But this is the only time where I get
to spend time with you guys.

34
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:47,130
You guys are the only ones who would
join a club with this weird goal.

35
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:51,530
This place is a special place for me!

36
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,960
Hey, what do you guys think?

37
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:56,760
Well, uhh...

38
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:58,240
What do you think, Inukawa?

39
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:02,960
Well, uhh, let's hear from
the youngest first.

40
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:05,990
Umm, telepathy is...

41
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:08,940
Sorry, what was our goal again?

42
00:02:16,870 --> 00:02:19,880
Wow, incredible lung capacity...

43
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:28,110
Thank you for everything, you three.

44
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:31,960
The Brainwave Club is hereby disbanded.

45
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,130
It was pretty fun.

46
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:40,230
Wait, we're really disbanded?

47
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:47,580
Seems like Kurata is way more serious
about this than we ever thought.

48
00:02:49,510 --> 00:02:54,360
I guess we should give
all the books in here a read?

49
00:03:00,450 --> 00:03:02,160
(MOB MOB WOW!)

50
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,030
(MOB MOB WOW!)

51
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,870
(MOB MOB WOW!)

52
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,710
(MOB MOB WOW!)

53
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,840
I realized that our youth is gray

54
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:17,760
The origin of this uneasiness
Is yet unknown

55
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,260
Trains of emotions keep running
Through my brain

56
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:23,430
Struggling through this adolescence

57
00:03:23,550 --> 00:03:26,390
Don't disturb my deep psyche

58
00:03:26,390 --> 00:03:29,060
Who is that behind you?

59
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:32,850
Opposing ideas create distortion

60
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:36,270
Exorcise all the sorrow

61
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,940
So, do what you can now

62
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:41,860
My life

63
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:45,990
Finally, break it down

64
00:03:47,490 --> 00:03:50,330
(Want) Both greed
(Young) And honesty

65
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:53,210
(Burn) Are growing
(1) On this chest of mine

66
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:55,960
(Trance) I'm not waking up
(Chance) I want to wake up

67
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:58,920
(Stance) These two different faces of mine
(1) Are standing back-to-back

68
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,420
Taking things as it is

69
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:04,840
In this free relation where
We resent each other

70
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:07,140
Once these two become one

71
00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:09,140
That smile becomes one

72
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:12,230
And only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

73
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:15,900
"1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

74
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:17,310
(MOB MOB WOW!)

75
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:20,190
One and only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

76
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,900
"1"

77
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,070
(MOB MOB WOW!)

78
00:04:23,070 --> 00:04:25,360
One and only "1"

79
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:31,450
(Communicating 1 ~Winter Break~)

80
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:36,740
Brother.

81
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:41,260
There's some guests for you.
They're waiting outside.

82
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:43,670
Who is it?

83
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:46,800
It seems pretty cold outside.

84
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:49,540
Are you okay?

85
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,900
What do you mean?

86
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:54,250
It's been a month since
Dimple last showed up.

87
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:55,920
Is it still bothering you?

88
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:58,900
Oh, I was just spacing off.

89
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:01,230
I see.

90
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:05,140
Huh?

91
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:07,210
Everyone? What's going on?

92
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:12,170
Mob! Why didn't you pick up your phone?
We called you several times!

93
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,450
Sorry, I didn't notice.

94
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,470
Did you need something?

95
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:20,280
Please, can't you use
your powers for telepathy?

96
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:24,250
We acted as if we knew
while we actually didn't!

97
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:26,830
We underestimated what
being a youth means!

98
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:29,070
Inukawa, calm down.

99
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,970
What is going on?

100
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:36,140
I see, so Tome quit.

101
00:05:36,450 --> 00:05:39,630
I think she's just prioritizing
her entrance exams.

102
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:43,400
But I can't use telepathy.

103
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,260
Can't you make it work somehow?

104
00:05:45,330 --> 00:05:48,860
Umm, I know someone
that can use telepathy.

105
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,630
Huh?

106
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:55,660
If the target is the space,
then I'm afraid we can't help.

107
00:05:55,850 --> 00:05:59,380
Our telepathy only works
between us siblings.

108
00:05:59,550 --> 00:06:00,920
I see.

109
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:04,140
Yeah, of course
it wouldn't be that easy...

110
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:05,760
But...

111
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:11,610
We might be able to find other telepaths
if someone stronger helped.

112
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:16,700
Yeah, but only if there is someone
who can receive our telepathy.

113
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:17,940
Huh?

114
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:22,010
It might be impossible to send
a specific message to someone,

115
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:25,210
but we can spread
a noise around us.

116
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,620
Noise?

117
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:30,550
It's an unpleasant sound
that only telepaths can hear.

118
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,390
So, something like an ear ringing?

119
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:35,030
So you're going to call them?

120
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:38,900
Yes, but it depends on the person
receiving it themselves.

121
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:44,660
If we keep emitting the noise, they might
try to approach the source of the noise.

122
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:47,260
But we won't know
what kind of person it is, then?

123
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:48,770
That's kinda scary, isn't it?

124
00:06:48,770 --> 00:06:52,220
But they're our only hope.

125
00:06:52,990 --> 00:06:55,100
What do we do, Brother?

126
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:58,390
This is for Tome, right?
Let's do it.

127
00:06:58,470 --> 00:07:00,480
What can I do to help?

128
00:07:00,570 --> 00:07:03,640
He seems really dependable
for some reason...

129
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:08,760
It's cold here, so how about we first move
to the club room for a strategy meeting?

130
00:07:10,450 --> 00:07:12,410
-Go go go!
-Pass here!

131
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:16,250
Right now, thank's to Teru's training,

132
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:20,080
we can communicate up to
three kilometers if we do our best.

133
00:07:20,250 --> 00:07:23,550
I managed to receive the message
to buy natto

134
00:07:23,550 --> 00:07:25,150
on the way home the other day.

135
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:28,300
You could've just used a phone
rather than trying hard.

136
00:07:28,450 --> 00:07:30,990
But if we fire the noise
in all directions,

137
00:07:30,990 --> 00:07:33,920
then we'll probably only
manage around 500 meters.

138
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:36,010
That's not very far...

139
00:07:36,090 --> 00:07:40,330
If Kageyama helps
and amplifies our output,

140
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:43,680
I think we can double
or triple our noise range.

141
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:46,350
Whoa, that's amazing.

142
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:49,650
Wait, is Mob's brother also a psychic?!

143
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,300
My brother would be better at this.

144
00:07:52,650 --> 00:07:56,910
Let's give it a try.
I'll try to make it as wide as possible.

145
00:07:57,110 --> 00:08:00,650
Thanks for calling us
for this interesting experiment.

146
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:03,830
We can finally pay you back,
Kageyama.

147
00:08:04,010 --> 00:08:06,290
All right, let's try this, Kaito.

148
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:09,430
Yeah. Let's do our best, Brother.

149
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:15,380
We're currently emitting the noise.

150
00:08:15,810 --> 00:08:18,240
We can't hear anything...

151
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:20,680
But yeah, do your thing, Mob.

152
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:28,100
I'm sending some power your way.

153
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:29,760
Please do.

154
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,720
T-this is amazing!

155
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,830
Even I can faintly hear it.

156
00:08:44,510 --> 00:08:46,960
I-it feels like my head
is about to split open!

157
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:50,550
I can add some more,
but I guess we shouldn't do that.

158
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:53,750
It's okay, we'll push it to the limit.

159
00:08:54,050 --> 00:08:55,720
You don't have to push
yourselves that far!

160
00:08:55,790 --> 00:08:58,040
This is the only way!

161
00:08:58,040 --> 00:09:00,040
Please do it!

162
00:09:02,930 --> 00:09:05,430
Whoa, I'm getting goosebumps.

163
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:06,950
Y-yeah, me too.

164
00:09:06,950 --> 00:09:09,420
Is it affecting the human body?

165
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:10,990
Who is it?

166
00:09:11,370 --> 00:09:13,700
Whoa, that scared me.

167
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:16,150
What are you guys doing here?

168
00:09:16,230 --> 00:09:18,580
Oh, it's just Takenaka.

169
00:09:18,750 --> 00:09:20,010
Who is he?

170
00:09:20,010 --> 00:09:22,300
A former member of the Brainwave Club.

171
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:26,120
The Brainwave Club was abolished
because he quit on us.

172
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:30,470
Why are you back here now, anyway?
You're in the Tennis Club, right?

173
00:09:30,590 --> 00:09:34,560
Oh, we still have club activities
even on winter break.

174
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:38,840
They're making us run around
the perimeters in this stupid cold weather.

175
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:42,680
I mean, that's what you signed up for.

176
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:45,610
So I waited for a chance to slip away.

177
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:48,920
I was thinking of taking it easy
in this room.

178
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,590
I knew it, you're actually just like us.

179
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,420
By the way, what are you doing?

180
00:09:55,530 --> 00:09:57,490
We're looking for telepaths.

181
00:09:57,490 --> 00:09:59,490
These people are psychics.

182
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:00,550
What?

183
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:02,530
Are you for real?

184
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,790
You guys are still doing
that kind of thing?

185
00:10:05,790 --> 00:10:07,030
That's so stupid!

186
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:11,650
This is why people think the Brainwave Club
is full of weirdos and creeps.

187
00:10:11,730 --> 00:10:13,880
Get a grip already.

188
00:10:13,930 --> 00:10:15,360
Oh, shut up.

189
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:18,440
We're just finally getting
serious now, okay?

190
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:20,600
If you're going to get in our way,
please leave.

191
00:10:20,710 --> 00:10:24,810
Fine, I'll leave once I warm myself a bit.

192
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:28,970
All right, let's do it one more time.

193
00:10:28,970 --> 00:10:31,230
It was going pretty well.

194
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:34,010
Yeah, if we do it multiple times
during this winter break,

195
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:37,620
a real telepath might actually show up.

196
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:39,450
All right, ready...

197
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,010
...go!

198
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:46,030
Hey, you self-proclaimed psychics.

199
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:49,680
What the heck are you guys doing
with such a serious face?

200
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:56,910
Aren't you guys embarrassed?

201
00:10:59,990 --> 00:11:01,910
It's getting even stronger?

202
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,760
Just a little more push.

203
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:08,460
Even my head starts to hurt.

204
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:13,920
Can't you guys just stop...?

205
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:17,050
What's wrong, Takenaka?
You're looking kinda pale.

206
00:11:17,210 --> 00:11:19,520
Do you have a fever or something?

207
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,560
You're so noisy, goddammit!

208
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,550
Just...

209
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:42,250
Just stop that noise already.

210
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:54,350
I find out I'm different from others
when I was five.

211
00:11:55,100 --> 00:12:02,240
The kindergarten teacher's thoughts and
speech are different, but nobody noticed.

212
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:05,500
Then when I voiced
my father's real thoughts,

213
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:07,420
my mother broke down crying.

214
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:10,390
That's when I realized it's not something
I'm supposed to do.

215
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:16,530
Others' thoughts just simply
came to my head.

216
00:12:16,730 --> 00:12:19,850
As I grew up,
they grow even louder,

217
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,650
and the range from where
I can receive them also grows.

218
00:12:22,650 --> 00:12:24,800
It was such a pain.

219
00:12:25,130 --> 00:12:30,520
I think it was around third grade
when I can send my thoughts to others.

220
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:35,810
You always carry snacks
with you, that's nice.

221
00:12:35,810 --> 00:12:39,790
I have tons of them back at home.
I'll bring some next time.

222
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,460
-Really? Then I want some crackling gum.
-I'll go shoplifting again.

223
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:47,750
Are you stupid?
You're going to get arrested!

224
00:12:49,470 --> 00:12:50,760
What's wrong?

225
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:52,670
Return it to the shop!

226
00:12:52,670 --> 00:12:55,020
O-okay!

227
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:59,840
After that, to let off some steam,

228
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:04,780
I assaulted someone by yelling
inside their head every day.

229
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:09,220
Y-you always lived like that?

230
00:13:09,610 --> 00:13:11,680
I don't do that anymore, Inukawa.

231
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,920
-Wha?!
-What's wrong?

232
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:16,810
He spoke... directly in my head?

233
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:19,030
Kijibayashi, Saruta.

234
00:13:21,030 --> 00:13:22,590
Really?

235
00:13:23,290 --> 00:13:27,360
He's kinda scary.
Telepaths are abnormal.

236
00:13:27,470 --> 00:13:29,580
Yeah, I guess so.

237
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:32,350
I am an abnormal existence.

238
00:13:32,350 --> 00:13:33,810
But don't worry.

239
00:13:33,810 --> 00:13:38,000
I've learned how to keep other's thoughts
from entering my head.

240
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:41,960
I've had enough of listening to what
others think. It makes me sick.

241
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:44,700
That's why I always wear an earplug.

242
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:47,320
I sealed this ability away.

243
00:13:47,630 --> 00:13:51,690
But then I hear this
really stupid loud noise.

244
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:55,130
Oh, right, sorry about that.

245
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:57,530
We're looking for telepaths.

246
00:13:57,530 --> 00:13:58,880
Will you help us?

247
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,860
Why now?

248
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,520
You're not actually interested
in telepathy, right?

249
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:05,400
No, we're serious here!

250
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,970
You'll know it's true
if you read our thoughts!

251
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:12,620
I don't want to make any more
bad memories with telepathy.

252
00:14:12,710 --> 00:14:15,210
I'm not going to take off
my earplug either.

253
00:14:15,210 --> 00:14:16,910
Go ask someone else.

254
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,790
You were looking for friends,
didn't you?

255
00:14:20,210 --> 00:14:21,400
What?

256
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,940
You joined this club

257
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:28,700
because you thought there might
be someone like you, right?

258
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:31,370
Yeah, that's right.

259
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:33,370
But that was a mistake.

260
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:35,520
It's just some occult research club.

261
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:42,520
That's why I stopped having the faint hope
that there is someone else like me.

262
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:48,620
I have no plan of being used to make
some "fun memories" for you people.

263
00:14:48,710 --> 00:14:50,350
Being used...

264
00:14:50,350 --> 00:14:54,700
If you think that's all there is to it,
then it's okay if you don't want to help.

265
00:14:55,070 --> 00:14:57,920
That is, if you really aren't interested.

266
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,080
What are you trying to say?

267
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:04,840
I also have times when
I'm fed up with my powers.

268
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:08,170
Even if I try to hide it,
it's still an inseparable part of me.

269
00:15:08,910 --> 00:15:10,760
If there are others that need your powers,

270
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:15,010
then I think accepting their request
can sometimes be enjoyable.

271
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:19,630
What's with the high and mighty act?
Don't act like you know me.

272
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,350
It's my true feeling.

273
00:15:30,010 --> 00:15:33,410
W-well, I don't want you
to make that noise again.

274
00:15:33,410 --> 00:15:36,410
I guess I'll help, just this once.

275
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:40,190
Thanks! We'll be in your debt,
Takenaka!

276
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:41,370
-Yay!
-Yay!

277
00:15:41,370 --> 00:15:43,790
-We did it!
-Thanks a lot, you two!

278
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,710
Takenaka.

279
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:49,820
Did you... read my brother's mind?

280
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,350
You're his little brother, huh?

281
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,360
Now then, did I?

282
00:15:53,470 --> 00:15:56,800
You have a complex about not being able
to relate with your brother?

283
00:15:56,890 --> 00:15:59,370
Is that what my thoughts are saying?!

284
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:01,760
Nah, I'm just guessing.

285
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:05,920
I have my earplugs, but I can still
guess somewhat from your eyes.

286
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:09,350
I think those kinds of things
should be cherished.

287
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:13,740
So, what am I supposed to do?

288
00:16:16,370 --> 00:16:17,520
Here.

289
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:21,200
It's a purifying kelp tea that we've
just begun accepting mail-order recently.

290
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:24,600
Winter also affects those
kinds of spiritual things,

291
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,830
so please make sure
to keep yourself hydrated.

292
00:16:26,830 --> 00:16:30,290
Dehydration leads
to poor blood circulation,

293
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:35,630
so it might invite evil spirits that cause
fatigue and poor sleeping habits.

294
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:37,390
Ooh...

295
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:39,730
Thank you very much.

296
00:16:39,730 --> 00:16:42,790
I will visit you again, Master Reigen.

297
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,810
Even my body feels sluggish.

298
00:16:48,950 --> 00:16:52,030
It's hard to get any motivation
when it's this cold, yeah?

299
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:53,920
What are you doing?

300
00:16:53,980 --> 00:16:58,010
It's homework from school.
I have to finish it during winter break.

301
00:16:58,010 --> 00:16:59,470
Winter break, huh?

302
00:16:59,470 --> 00:17:02,580
Being a student sure is nice,
having events like that and all.

303
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,450
How about we go drinking for once?

304
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:10,740
Sorry, I have a year-end party
with friends from night school today.

305
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:12,280
I see...

306
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:17,070
Oh, Mob? What's wrong?

307
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:20,980
Plans for New Year's Eve?
I don't have any for now.

308
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:23,220
Are you going on a shrine visit
on New Year?

309
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,620
What?

310
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:26,270
Mud Boat Mountain?

311
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:28,040
UFO?

312
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:32,320
Fine, fine. I'll do it.

313
00:17:35,330 --> 00:17:38,380
I gotta go for some UFO searching
at the end of the year.

314
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:42,570
They called me just so they
could get me to rent a car.

315
00:17:42,730 --> 00:17:48,110
Man, why do I have to babysit
on New Year's Eve?

316
00:17:48,270 --> 00:17:50,870
I'm happy for you, Reigen.

317
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:54,140
What? Mud Boat Mountain?

318
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:55,990
I'm not going.

319
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,300
Got a winter training camp
with my cram school.

320
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,330
The Brainwave Club is already
disbanded anyway,

321
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:02,860
just do whatever you want.

322
00:18:05,190 --> 00:18:06,710
She said she isn't coming...

323
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:09,530
Seriously, President Kurata?

324
00:18:09,610 --> 00:18:13,100
I guess we just have to keep
inviting her until New Year's Eve.

325
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:15,070
She'll definitely agree eventually.

326
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:21,160
However, President Kurata stopped
answering her phone after that.

327
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:26,250
And so, New Year's Eve arrives.

328
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:33,370
That's a weirdly nice sleep,
I even woke up on my own...

329
00:18:35,430 --> 00:18:36,380
Huh?

330
00:18:36,530 --> 00:18:40,000
It ran out of batteries?!
You got to be kidding me!

331
00:18:40,060 --> 00:18:43,480
I lectured Mob to always be punctual,
and now look at me!

332
00:18:45,230 --> 00:18:47,560
What, Tome isn't coming?

333
00:18:47,930 --> 00:18:49,080
Yeah...

334
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:51,570
We ended up losing contact with her.

335
00:18:51,570 --> 00:18:54,990
But I'm sure she'll be happy
if we show her some UFO photos.

336
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,410
You're right.

337
00:18:56,610 --> 00:18:59,580
We've made it this far,
let's make sure we find those UFOs.

338
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:05,760
She's actually here.

339
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:07,890
Faster than anybody else, to boot.

340
00:19:08,010 --> 00:19:10,320
What's this all about,
President Kurata?

341
00:19:10,390 --> 00:19:11,990
What about your training camp?

342
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:14,280
Yeah, I'm skipping that.

343
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:17,240
What, am I not supposed to be here?

344
00:19:17,350 --> 00:19:18,550
No, but...

345
00:19:18,550 --> 00:19:20,920
Why didn't you answer your phone?

346
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,320
Oh, that? I broke my phone,
so I didn't realize.

347
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:26,150
The heck?

348
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:30,140
So, who's the telepath you guys found?

349
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:32,090
She still doesn't know?

350
00:19:32,090 --> 00:19:34,560
Yeah, I thought she wouldn't
come if we told her.

351
00:19:34,890 --> 00:19:37,480
The meeting time is 9 AM, right?

352
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:39,440
Let's wait for a little bit.

353
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:44,820
Right, they're totally not coming.

354
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:48,640
Why won't he pick up his phone?!

355
00:19:50,490 --> 00:19:54,040
Is it okay to make
your master wait this long?

356
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:55,930
I'm not sure.

357
00:19:55,930 --> 00:19:57,950
I sent a message telling
the situation earlier,

358
00:19:57,950 --> 00:19:59,510
but he didn't reply.

359
00:19:59,630 --> 00:20:02,130
We might have to call this off...

360
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,860
You're so freaking late, Takenaka!

361
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,930
My bad, I overslept.

362
00:20:09,110 --> 00:20:10,760
Takenaka?

363
00:20:10,970 --> 00:20:13,110
What the heck are you doing here?

364
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:15,970
Sorry I'm late.

365
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:17,840
President Kurata.

366
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,300
I'm the telepath.

367
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:22,250
What?

368
00:20:22,250 --> 00:20:25,720
What is this?
Are you guys messing with me?

369
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:30,640
Well, now that everyone's here,
let's head to the parking lot.

370
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:31,920
Run for it!!

371
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:35,330
Hurry up! He might be angry
and already left!

372
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:37,950
He's here!

373
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:41,730
I'm sorry we took a while, Master.

374
00:20:41,820 --> 00:20:44,320
Oh, don't worry about it.

375
00:20:44,430 --> 00:20:48,170
It's New Year's Eve,
let's take it easy.

376
00:20:48,410 --> 00:20:50,770
He just arrived two minutes ago.

377
00:20:53,550 --> 00:20:56,550
O-okay, let's go.

378
00:20:56,750 --> 00:20:59,240
Please drive safely.

379
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:03,450
Please don't talk for a while.

380
00:21:07,510 --> 00:21:10,890
How could you oversleep on
an important day like this?

381
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,690
I had a hard time sleeping.

382
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:16,350
Was others' thought too loud again?

383
00:21:16,460 --> 00:21:18,440
No, I was nervous.

384
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:20,720
It's been a while since
I've done anything like this.

385
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,480
I see.

386
00:21:22,860 --> 00:21:26,510
-President, do you want some gum?
-Hmph, no.

387
00:21:26,890 --> 00:21:29,100
Can't believe you guys
actually tricked me.

388
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:31,430
Takenaka's a telepath? Hah.

389
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:34,190
-No, he's the real deal.
-It's okay.

390
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:38,060
I don't even know if I can call
a UFO or not either.

391
00:21:40,570 --> 00:21:43,210
Approaching destination.

392
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:45,340
Oh, so this is the place?

393
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:47,360
It's Mud Boat Mountain.

394
00:21:47,470 --> 00:21:49,950
It's going to be full of winding
mountain roads from here.

395
00:21:49,950 --> 00:21:53,460
Don't get carsick before
we find the UFO, okay?

396
00:21:55,370 --> 00:22:00,210
The blue light shined
Dazzling my eye at 01:30 AM

397
00:22:00,250 --> 00:22:05,590
Even as I swiped the page over,
The smiles of friends besides me remain

398
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,020
Yes, I want someone to understand

399
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:20,520
All the colorless and transparent wishes

400
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:23,020
All the breath stuck within
The depth of my heart

401
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:25,650
Suddenly flowed out
Bringing my consciousness back

402
00:22:25,650 --> 00:22:28,110
I remember the days hung dry

403
00:22:28,110 --> 00:22:30,620
The very normal days passed by

404
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:33,080
Even if reality is corrupted

405
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:35,830
The sky we saw together
Was definitely real

406
00:22:36,410 --> 00:22:40,540
It's harder to understand than
The grammar on the blackboard

407
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:45,760
The story that disappears
Under 24 hours makes me sad and lonely

408
00:22:46,010 --> 00:22:50,220
It's so hard, and I find myself
On the verge of giving up again and again

409
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:51,760
But I...

410
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:55,930
The current me will no longer give up

411
00:22:56,060 --> 00:23:00,940
Overflowing emotions on my sleeve,
Running through worry and doubt

412
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:03,573
Nobody has decided
if the future is 0 or 100,

413
00:23:03,575 --> 00:23:06,150
So I'll paint over them myself

414
00:23:06,150 --> 00:23:08,541
Even if my existence itself
can't be proven,

415
00:23:08,543 --> 00:23:11,571
If this world struck me in my heart

416
00:23:11,700 --> 00:23:14,240
I will flood it with cobalt blue

417
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:27,960
Hysteria from carsickness
and forgetting to bring things.

418
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:30,060
Many things happened,
but we reached the summit.

419
00:23:30,060 --> 00:23:32,500
Now, time to show the power
of the Brainwave Club!

420
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:34,610
Next on episode eight of
Mob Psycho 100 III,

421
00:23:34,610 --> 00:23:36,760
"Communicating 2
~Close Encounters of the Third Kind~"

422
00:23:36,870 --> 00:23:39,870
Watching from overseas?
Of course, that is a wise decision.
